, "JnXvu0": {"type":"text","parent":"JRMkx0","order":"a2","name":"Intro","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"Editing a text keeps it exactly where and how it is drawn: same box width, same wrapping, same font, size, line height, letter spacing and alignment — entering or leaving edit mode never reflows it, at any zoom. Inside the box, part of the text can carry its own style, as in Figma: select characters and change family, weight, size, color, italic, underline, strikethrough, letter spacing, line height or link — only that range changes. The file stores such a text as spans (feature text/runs) and falls back to a plain string when every span looks the same. Closed by a rules table.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-lg"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

