, "O57flR": {"type":"text","parent":"x6J4cQ","order":"a1","name":"Spec","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"Frames carry the system icon treatment; only rotation and glow change. macOS 26 draws the idle app icon with a glass rim, plate depth and a shaded mark, but an NSDockTile content view gets none of it, so every frame does: outside a 66 px radius (at 256 px) each frame is the idle icon pixel for pixel, inside it the IconServices rendering of that rotation, with the bloom composited behind the mark. Frame 0 is the idle icon itself. macOS before 26 (flat icons) plays flat frames.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-xs"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

