, "RiZri0": {"type":"text","parent":"sEtuu0","order":"a2","name":"Intro","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"While any agent is working — a built-in Agent turn in any window, or an MCP client with a tools/call in flight or an edit in the last 2 s — the macOS Dock tile plays a 2 s loop: the spiked outer shape of the mark turns clockwise and the pucker opening turns counter-clockwise, one 60° symmetry step per beat, with a soft white bloom behind the mark that swells with the motion. Every frame carries the icon treatment macOS 26 gives the idle app icon (glass rim, plate depth, shaded mark), so only the rotation and the glow change. Idle, the tile is the normal icon and nothing runs.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-lg"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

