, "S3rXk0": {"type":"text","parent":"j5XBa0","order":"a2","name":"Intro","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"While an agent works, the canvas shows two things per agent: one cursor (pointer + name pill) floating in the middle of the section it is editing, and a thin outline on that section. Nothing else: no shimmer, tint or skeleton, no placeholder or attribution tags, no outlines on small layers. The built-in agent and external MCP clients follow the same rules. This board supersedes the conflicting canvas rules on boards 21, 22, 24, 31 and 35.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-lg"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

