, "VZBje0": {"type":"text","parent":"GrMlI0","order":"a2","name":"Intro","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"Layers an agent adds grow into place instead of popping in. Each new layer fades in, scales up from 96 % and rises 6 px over 200 ms. Its auto-layout siblings and parents slide to their new boxes over the same 200 ms. A batch from an MCP client reveals one layer after another in document order. The motion is drawn by the renderer only: the document holds the final values from the first frame, so exports, kimo_render, thumbnails and hit testing never see an in-between state. The landing flash ring stays as it is.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-lg"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

