, "VyRJu0": {"type":"text","parent":"JCQwA0","order":"a2","name":"Intro","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"A per-session switch for the built-in agent and a per-client option for MCP clients. While it is on, every approval request is approved at once: file open, create, save and export, edits outside the agent's area and document-wide changes. Each one is still written down, as a line in the thread and a row in Activity. Safety limits that are not approvals stay in force. The approval prompt also gets a height cap so a request with many changes never runs off the screen.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-lg"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

