, "ZV98t0": {"type":"text","parent":"OiISW0","order":"a1","name":"Spec","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"Move to Trash sends the file to the OS Trash (Rust kimo_trash) and records original path, trashed path, name and time in ~/.kimo/trash.json. Restore moves it back, or offers Restore as copy when the name is taken. Delete forever and Empty trash delete only indexed items, after a confirm. Rows whose trashed file is gone are dropped on load. Kimo never empties the Trash on its own.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-xs"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

