, "mk1l10": {"type":"text","parent":"DALyB0","order":"a2","name":"Intro","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"The built-in agent can search the web and read pages when a task needs outside facts, such as a current font stack, a brand color or a product's copy. It is on by default: a setting in AI providers sets it for new sessions and the Web access switch in the composer's “…” menu turns it off for one session. No third-party fetch turns it off everywhere. Each search and each page read is a step in the thread and a row in Activity, and the reply ends with the links it used.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-lg"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

