, "xOgs10": {"type":"text","parent":"ZJ55a0","order":"a1","name":"Spec","w":{"mode":"fill"},"content":"kimo_apply_ops from any agent (built-in panel, Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, any MCP client) refuses a call whose insert ops author more than 40 new layers (AGENT_MAX_NEW_LAYERS): BATCH_TOO_LARGE with {limit, newLayers} and a split suggestion; nothing is applied. The limit is a ceiling, not a target. Copies, duplicates, page duplicates and component instances are never limited, whatever their size. Edits to existing layers are not limited. User actions (paste, import, duplicate) never go through it.","grow":"fixed-width","style":{"font":{"$ref":"font-sans"},"size":{"$ref":"text-xs"},"weight":400,"lineHeight":1.45},"fill":{"$ref":"text-secondary"}}

